#: docs/specifications/domain/design.md
msgid "How contexts map onto the platform"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/design.md
msgid "**One steward per context.** Each context owns the catalogs of its resources (below) and is stewarded by one role."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/design.md
msgid "**A product sits inside one context.** Its repository, operational database and tenant entry belong to that context. A product that needs another context's data uses that context's published interfaces."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/design.md
msgid "**Contexts integrate only through published interfaces:** registry interfaces, domain events, and gold tables with their semantic-layer definitions. No product reads another context's operational database ([CAP-INTEROPERABILITY.8]{1})."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/design.md
msgid "**The language follows the boundary.** A term means what its context's `CONTEXT.md` says; where two contexts use one word differently, each defines it, and translation happens at the interface between them."
msgstr ""
